.TH XUR.STD.MEM 7 "2026-10-27" "xur 0.1.1" "Xur Manual"
.SH NAME
xur.std.mem \- struct size, alignment and binary conversion
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B use std::mem;
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B std::mem
provides size and alignment queries and binary conversion for structs
that have a layout (see
.BR xur.std.reflect (7)
for the layout system).
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.B size_of::<T>() -> i64
The size in bytes of
.IR T .
.TP
.B align_of::<T>() -> i64
The alignment of
.IR T .
.TP
.B size_of_val(value) -> i64
The size in bytes of a struct value.
.TP
.B from_bytes::<T>(data) -> T
Read a struct of type
.I T
from the start of
.IR data .
.TP
.B to_bytes(value) -> bytes
Serialize a struct value to bytes.
.SH STRUCT METHODS
Every struct value also has:
.TP
.B value.to_bytes() -> bytes
Serialize the struct to bytes using its layout.
.TP
.B value.byte_size() -> i64
The struct's size in bytes.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
use std::mem;
use std::io;

#[repr(C)]
struct Header { magic: u32, version: u16 }

fn main() {
    io::println("size: {}", mem::size_of::<Header>());
    let h = Header { magic: 0x5a4d, version: 1 };
    let data = h.to_bytes();
    io::println("bytes: {}", data.to_hex());
}
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xur.std (7),
.BR xur.std.reflect (7),
.BR xur.std.bytes (7)
